1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,520
Three winter months in Korea:

2
00:00:03,520 --> 00:00:05,140
snowy palace roofs

3
00:00:05,140 --> 00:00:06,460
Seoul lights

4
00:00:06,460 --> 00:00:08,640
mountain festivals and hot street food

5
00:00:08,640 --> 00:00:10,920
plus the packing advice to enjoy them.

6
00:00:11,298 --> 00:00:14,118
Here are the places and regions we will cover.

7
00:00:14,964 --> 00:00:16,524
Pack for the cold

8
00:00:16,524 --> 00:00:18,484
and the season opens up.

9
00:00:19,326 --> 00:00:19,941
First

10
00:00:19,941 --> 00:00:23,556
pack for below-freezing nights in Seoul.

11
00:00:23,556 --> 00:00:25,864
Take a warm padded coat

12
00:00:25,864 --> 00:00:27,940
thermal layers, gloves

13
00:00:27,940 --> 00:00:28,633
a hat

14
00:00:28,633 --> 00:00:32,086
a scarf and shoes with good grip.

15
00:00:32,976 --> 00:00:34,056
Second

16
00:00:34,056 --> 00:00:37,656
check the forecast a few days before you leave.

17
00:00:37,656 --> 00:00:39,436
Averages are not a prediction

18
00:00:39,436 --> 00:00:42,396
and a cold snap or strong wind can change

19
00:00:42,396 --> 00:00:43,556
how the day feels.

20
00:00:44,846 --> 00:00:47,086
These are the three cities to compare.

21
00:00:47,940 --> 00:00:49,540
In Seoul

22
00:00:49,540 --> 00:00:51,680
average daytime highs are about two to five

23
00:00:51,680 --> 00:00:55,100
degrees from December through February.

24
00:00:55,100 --> 00:00:57,180
Average night lows range from about minus

25
00:00:57,180 --> 00:00:59,120
three to minus six

26
00:00:59,120 --> 00:01:01,060
with January coldest.

27
00:01:01,446 --> 00:01:04,786
Cold waves can push Seoul down to minus ten

28
00:01:04,786 --> 00:01:07,326
degrees or lower at night.

29
00:01:07,326 --> 00:01:10,166
The dry north-westerly wind can make it feel

30
00:01:10,166 --> 00:01:13,146
several degrees colder than the thermometer says.

31
00:01:13,656 --> 00:01:15,956
Busan is milder:

32
00:01:15,956 --> 00:01:18,436
average highs sit around eight to ten degrees

33
00:01:18,436 --> 00:01:20,456
and lows around zero to two.

34
00:01:20,456 --> 00:01:22,916
It can still feel windy by the sea.

35
00:01:23,274 --> 00:01:26,214
Jeju is also milder than Seoul

36
00:01:26,214 --> 00:01:29,914
with average highs around nine to eleven degrees.

37
00:01:29,914 --> 00:01:31,294
It can be windy

38
00:01:31,294 --> 00:01:34,434
and winter flights may be delayed by wind or snow.

39
00:01:34,884 --> 00:01:38,824
Snow falls a few times most winters in Seoul

40
00:01:38,824 --> 00:01:40,784
usually lightly.

41
00:01:40,784 --> 00:01:42,424
Gangwon Province gets more

42
00:01:42,424 --> 00:01:44,224
and days are short:

43
00:01:44,224 --> 00:01:45,244
in December

44
00:01:45,244 --> 00:01:47,424
it gets dark around half past five.

45
00:01:47,838 --> 00:01:51,218
Here are three Seoul stops that show winter in

46
00:01:51,218 --> 00:01:51,898
the city.

47
00:01:52,392 --> 00:01:54,972
If snow falls

48
00:01:54,972 --> 00:01:58,052
head to Gyeongbokgung or Changdeokgung early.

49
00:01:58,052 --> 00:02:00,712
Snow on the curved palace roofs is beautiful

50
00:02:00,712 --> 00:02:02,492
but the paths may be cleared as the day

51
00:02:02,492 --> 00:02:03,292
goes on.

52
00:02:03,810 --> 00:02:06,030
From late November

53
00:02:06,030 --> 00:02:08,190
Seoul's department stores

54
00:02:08,190 --> 00:02:11,570
shopping streets and squares put on lights.

55
00:02:11,570 --> 00:02:13,550
Take an evening walk through the city

56
00:02:13,550 --> 00:02:16,330
then warm up with a hot snack.

57
00:02:16,716 --> 00:02:20,294
New Year's Eve brings bell ringing at Bosingak.

58
00:02:20,294 --> 00:02:22,403
For winter comfort any day

59
00:02:22,403 --> 00:02:23,744
look for hotteok

60
00:02:23,744 --> 00:02:25,022
fish-shaped buns

61
00:02:25,022 --> 00:02:29,156
roasted sweet potatoes or fish cakes in hot broth.

62
00:02:29,622 --> 00:02:33,102
Ski resorts and winter festivals are the big

63
00:02:33,102 --> 00:02:35,282
draws in the colder mountains.

64
00:02:35,832 --> 00:02:38,706
Korea's ski season runs roughly from December

65
00:02:38,706 --> 00:02:39,736
to early March.

66
00:02:39,736 --> 00:02:42,718
Resorts are within an easy day trip of Seoul

67
00:02:42,718 --> 00:02:45,538
and shuttle buses and English-speaking rental

68
00:02:45,538 --> 00:02:48,332
counters make a first ski day simpler.

69
00:02:49,098 --> 00:02:50,998
In January

70
00:02:50,998 --> 00:02:53,958
the Hwacheon Sancheoneo Ice Festival is known

71
00:02:53,958 --> 00:02:56,798
for fishing through holes in a frozen river

72
00:02:56,798 --> 00:02:59,278
then having the catch grilled on the spot.

73
00:03:00,156 --> 00:03:03,276
Pyeongchang also holds a trout festival around

74
00:03:03,276 --> 00:03:05,236
the same time.

75
00:03:05,236 --> 00:03:07,296
Festival dates depend on the ice and are

76
00:03:07,296 --> 00:03:08,696
announced in autumn

77
00:03:08,696 --> 00:03:11,136
so check the official website before booking.

78
00:03:11,718 --> 00:03:15,878
These two stops offer a taste of winter beyond

79
00:03:15,878 --> 00:03:17,478
Seoul and the mountains.

80
00:03:17,928 --> 00:03:19,848
On the east coast

81
00:03:19,848 --> 00:03:23,568
winter and early spring are snow crab season.

82
00:03:23,568 --> 00:03:25,968
Yeongdeok and Uljin are among the towns

83
00:03:25,968 --> 00:03:27,468
serving it steamed

84
00:03:27,468 --> 00:03:30,748
with crab butter mixed into fried rice at the end.

85
00:03:31,098 --> 00:03:33,498
Jeju is milder than the mainland.

86
00:03:33,498 --> 00:03:36,498
Look for camellias and seasonal tangerines;

87
00:03:36,498 --> 00:03:38,538
Hallasan may be snow-covered

88
00:03:38,538 --> 00:03:41,418
so a winter hike needs proper gear.

89
00:03:41,868 --> 00:03:43,588
For a ski day

90
00:03:43,588 --> 00:03:46,008
shuttle buses from Seoul can make getting to a

91
00:03:46,008 --> 00:03:48,028
resort straightforward.

92
00:03:48,028 --> 00:03:49,628
Confirm the current schedule and booking

93
00:03:49,628 --> 00:03:51,548
details before you travel.

94
00:03:51,918 --> 00:03:56,278
Keep plans flexible if you are flying to Jeju.

95
00:03:56,278 --> 00:03:58,758
Wind or snow can delay flights

96
00:03:58,758 --> 00:04:01,258
and mountain trails may close or require

97
00:04:01,258 --> 00:04:03,418
crampons after snowfall.

98
00:04:03,768 --> 00:04:06,488
Korea's heating is strong indoors

99
00:04:06,488 --> 00:04:08,128
so layers are useful:

100
00:04:08,128 --> 00:04:10,368
take one off when you step inside.

101
00:04:10,368 --> 00:04:13,168
The air is dry outside and in heated rooms

102
00:04:13,168 --> 00:04:15,828
so pack lip balm and moisturiser.

103
00:04:16,338 --> 00:04:20,018
Hand warmers are sold in convenience stores.

104
00:04:20,018 --> 00:04:22,458
Keep one in a pocket for outdoor sightseeing

105
00:04:22,458 --> 00:04:25,738
especially when the wind makes a cold day feel harsher.

106
00:04:26,292 --> 00:04:30,372
Some winter days are hazy with fine dust.

107
00:04:30,372 --> 00:04:32,252
Check an air quality app before planning a

108
00:04:32,252 --> 00:04:33,312
long day outside

109
00:04:33,312 --> 00:04:36,312
and check the weather again before mountain walks.

110
00:04:36,846 --> 00:04:39,646
Avoid these four winter surprises.

111
00:04:40,800 --> 00:04:44,120
Walk carefully on icy pavements

112
00:04:44,120 --> 00:04:45,940
steps and hills.

113
00:04:45,940 --> 00:04:46,840
Around Seollal

114
00:04:46,840 --> 00:04:51,380
some shops close and trains or buses can sell out.

115
00:04:51,380 --> 00:04:55,360
Check trail conditions and use crampons if required.

116
00:04:55,360 --> 00:04:57,720
Snow crab prices change with the catch.

117
00:04:58,170 --> 00:05:01,110
How cold is Seoul?

118
00:05:01,110 --> 00:05:04,550
Average daytime highs are about two to five degrees

119
00:05:04,550 --> 00:05:08,910
and average nights about minus three to minus six.

120
00:05:08,910 --> 00:05:11,590
Cold snaps can reach minus ten or lower.

121
00:05:11,988 --> 00:05:14,908
Is winter a good time to visit?

122
00:05:14,908 --> 00:05:15,328
Yes

123
00:05:15,328 --> 00:05:18,448
if you like crisp weather, lights, skiing

124
00:05:18,448 --> 00:05:20,148
festivals and warming food

125
00:05:20,148 --> 00:05:22,248
and do not mind packing for the cold.

126
00:05:22,686 --> 00:05:25,246
Does it snow in Seoul?

127
00:05:25,246 --> 00:05:27,186
A few times most winters

128
00:05:27,186 --> 00:05:28,726
usually lightly.

129
00:05:28,726 --> 00:05:32,126
The mountains of Gangwon Province get far more snow.

130
00:05:32,736 --> 00:05:34,636
The short version:

131
00:05:34,636 --> 00:05:37,476
pack warm layers and shoes with grip

132
00:05:37,476 --> 00:05:39,036
check the forecast

133
00:05:39,036 --> 00:05:40,576
enjoy Seoul's lights and food

134
00:05:40,576 --> 00:05:43,716
and head to the mountains for snow or festivals.

135
00:05:44,394 --> 00:05:45,508
